  "term": "posterior pituitary",
  "definition": "The posterior pituitary, or neurohypophysis, is the back part of the pituitary gland where certain peptide hormones made by neurons in the hypothalamus are stored in nerve endings. When stimulated, it releases these hormones into the blood.",
